CLEVELAND, Ohio -- The Northeast Ohio Sewer District plans to use green approaches on 10 projects designed to help keep rainwater and untreated sewage from flooding into Lake Erie and surrounding waterways during storms.
Many of the projects will employ retention basins – dry man-made ponds – to capture rainwater during big storms before the water reaches the storm sewers. The basins allow the rain to evaporate or seep into the ground.
